          "note": "The recorded Report is the static scan plus Live Probe outcomes written by `dpdp-audit probe` against a clean copy of the pinned revision. The deliverable Report remains the static scan alone. The outcomes sit on the Consent Assessment criteria (`live_probes`, `live_probe_run`) and create no Finding; Replay Mode shows past results. The disposable Django instance ran in debug mode on loopback HTTP with a throwaway signing key and fresh SQLite so no real accounts or data were used. It raised the signup limit from 3/h per IP (finance_tracker/settings.py:419-425) to 100/h to create the run's accounts; rate limiting was not under test. It required email verification and used a file mailbox to verify synthetic accounts without sending mail. It used PostHog SDK 3.25.0 (the pin requires posthog>=3.5.0; 8.1.0 changed capture and removed module-level identify), a synthetic PostHog key and a run-scoped loopback sink to observe only this run's analytics without external delivery.",
